  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forest Guards Training for Conservation of Western Hoolock Gibbon in the state of Nagaland, India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">, (1) educate, expose and inculcate interest through various methods in Forest Guards to protect hoolock gibbon habitats in Nagaland and to educate them about global, national and local importance of the species; (2) train Forest guards to identify the different primate species and also to classify individuals based on age and sex to facilitate individual identification to maintain individual histories; (3) teach and train the Forest Guards about general primate survey, hoolock gibbon population estimates and their present status; and, (4) provide legal provisions concerning wildlife act and wildlife laws to contain wildlife crimes..</narrative>
  </description>
